# What the medium's own repository carries, so that a machine can be installed
# with no network at all, as Installation ISO decides.
#
# It is the bootstrap package set of Installer Inputs and Bootstrap Baseline,
# and every package it may install rather than the ones a given answer picks:
# an installation without a network cannot go and fetch the microcode of the
# processor it turns out to be running on. Their dependencies come with them,
# resolved when the medium is built.
#
# The project's own packages are added to this repository too, so that what an
# installation puts into the target comes from the medium when there is nothing
# to fetch from.

base
linux
linux-headers
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio
btrfs-progs
cryptsetup
grub
efibootmgr
sudo
networkmanager
ipxe

# Only when the answers ask for them, and therefore all of them
zram-generator
intel-ucode
amd-ucode
nvidia-open
plymouth

# What the tools this system installs need on it
oparch-return-message-render
oparch-dotfiles-sync
oparch-assets
oparch-keyring
